/S /P
/ActualText (Online data collection is gathering personal info through websites, apps, or online services.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [1]
>>
endobj
166 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (2. How do companies collect personal data online?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [2]
>>
endobj
167 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Companies collect data through forms, cookies, tracking pixels, and social media plugins.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [3]
>>
endobj
168 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (3. What are cookies and tracking pixels?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [4]
>>
endobj
169 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Cookies are small files stored on your device, while tracking pixels are small images that track your online activities.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [5]
>>
endobj
170 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (4. Can companies collect personal data without consent?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [6]
>>
endobj
171 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (No, companies need your explicit consent to collect your personal data.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [7]
>>
endobj
172 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (5. How must companies inform individuals about online data collection?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [8]
>>
endobj
173 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Companies must clearly explain what data they collect, why, and how they use it.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [9]
>>
endobj
174 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (6. What is the purpose of online data collection?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [10]
>>
endobj
175 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (Online data collection helps improve user experience, provide targeted ads, and gather analytics.)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [11]
>>
endobj
176 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/ActualText (7. Can individuals opt-out of online data collection?)
/Pg 11 0 R
/K [12]
>>
endobj
177 0 obj
<<
